<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $148.1 mln Sept 13.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $148.1 mln Sept 13.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $148.1 million surplus on Sept. 13 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON SEPTEMBER 13</p>
<p>Exports: $304.3 million</p>
<p>Imports: $173.5 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $135.1 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $117.8 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $148.1 million</p>
<p>SEPTEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.196 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.570 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.305 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.018 billion</p>
<p>Net deficit: $87 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
